  "Solution": "In option D, \\(\\angle C=180^\\circ-40^\\circ-70^\\circ=70^\\circ=\\angle B\\), so the triangle is isosceles. In A, the angles are \\(30^\\circ,50^\\circ,100^\\circ\\); in B, \\(50^\\circ,60^\\circ,70^\\circ\\); and in C, \\(20^\\circ,60^\\circ,100^\\circ\\). Each of those triples has three unequal angles. Thus D is correct.",
